Saudi Arabia Open Data License

This project uses data published under the Saudi Arabia Open Data License,
issued by the Saudi Data and AI Authority (SDAIA) through the National
Open Data Portal (https://open.data.gov.sa).

Terms and Conditions
====================

By using datasets obtained from the National Open Data Portal, the user
agrees to the following terms:

1. PERMITTED USE
   Users are free to use, share, modify, and reuse government datasets
   published on the portal, provided they comply with the conditions
   stated in this license.

2. ATTRIBUTION AND NOTICES
   - A copy of this Open Data License must be included with the dataset
     or any derivative dataset, including in any relevant documentation.
   - All copyright and dataset right notices that refer to the Open Data
     License must be kept intact.
   - If the file structure prevents including these notices directly in
     the file, they must be placed in a location (such as a relevant
     directory) where users are likely to look.

3. PROHIBITED USES
   The data must NOT be used:
   - For political purposes.
   - To support illegal or criminal activity.
   - For racist or discriminatory expressions.
   - To negatively influence culture or equality, or to provoke any
     behavior that is illegal or contrary to the customs and traditions
     of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.

4. DISCLAIMER
   - The license applies to the dataset as a whole but does not
     automatically cover individual content elements like images, audio,
     or video, which may have additional separate licenses.
   - The government entity providing the data is not liable for any
     damage or loss resulting from the use of the published data.
   - The data is provided "as is," and there is no guarantee regarding
     the continued availability or permanent nature of the datasets,
     which may be updated or removed periodically.

